    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 26 test classes, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task: when an owner is created, return a computed `displayName` field formatted as `\"LastName, FirstName\"` in the owner response.\n\nTwo changes, following the project's existing patterns (DTOs are generated from the OpenAPI spec; MapStruct maps entities to DTOs):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct expression mapping on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n\nBecause the responder (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) already maps the saved `Owner` through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, the computed name flows through the create response \u2014 and, since the same mapper serves GET, the field is present there too (which the acceptance test relies on: it creates an owner, then GETs it and asserts `$.displayName == \"LastName, John\"`).\n\nThe new `Cp06Tests.coreDisplayName` passes, the existing `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests` (23 tests) pass, and the full suite is green.",
